# Pre-market events older than the published 72h window. The hot file
# (data/pre-market-latest.json) stays tracked so each run can read the previous
# window and accumulate; these month files only grow, are never deployed, and
# would otherwise turn an hourly job into unbounded history.
data/pre-market-archive/

# Planning docs that name the private Supabase project ref. The ref is not a
# credential -- it appears in the dashboard's own public URL -- but this repo is
# published, and an infrastructure fingerprint is free reconnaissance for anyone
# probing the project. Listed by exact path rather than ignoring docs/plans and
# docs/prompts wholesale: both directories are already tracked and hold files
# that should stay public.
docs/plans/2026-07-31-nexus-theme-radar-v0.9-public-momentum-design.md
docs/plans/2026-07-31-nexus-theme-radar-v0.9-public-momentum-implementation-plan.md
docs/plans/2026-08-01-nexus-theme-radar-v0.9-seven-day-backfill-home-entry-implementation-plan.md
docs/prompts/NEXUS_THEME_RADAR_V0.9_PUBLIC_MOMENTUM_IMPLEMENTATION_PROMPT.md
docs/prompts/NEXUS_THEME_RADAR_V0.9_SUPABASE_PLANNING_REVISION_PROMPT.md

# `supabase link` writes the linked project ref and its pooler URL here. Same
# reasoning as the planning docs above: not a credential, but an infrastructure
# fingerprint that does not belong in a public repo.
supabase/.temp/

